{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghc34f91J3GAiuZDLzWA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QgqKcp1kXjEV5J9fRter7T","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/vv/zyff93v5391cmw7j8mlcf1ym0000gn/T/wi-agent-ptoywky0/NOTES.md","content":"# Algorithm\n\nLet s = x[1] + x[5] + x[9] + x[14], an integer from 0 to 4. The label is s mod 2.\n\n- **Layer 1:** units 0..3 compute r_k = relu(s - k) for k = 0, 1, 2, 3. Each has weight 1 on the four relevant bits and bias -k. All other units are zero.\n- **Layer 2:** for integer s in [0, 4], parity is exactly `odd = r0 - 2 r1 + 2 r2 - 2 r3`. Checking each value: s=0→0, s=1→1, s=2→0, s=3→1, s=4→0. Unit 0 = relu(odd) and unit 1 = relu(1 - odd). Both values are already 0 or 1, so the ReLU changes nothing.\n- **Output:** logit1 = 10·odd and logit0 = 10·(1 − odd). The argmax is the parity, with a margin of 10. The distractor bits have zero weight everywhere.\n\nThe network should be 100% accurate on all 2^16 inputs.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":458,"cache_read_input_tokens":5338,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":458},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"857c3b3b-b51a-4316-91ca-4115de2c5c29","uuid":"208d583e-c0d5-42c6-9f20-b648d4b2a1ec","timestamp":"2026-11-04T08:53:15.274Z","request_id":"req_011Cghc34FLbqyKGCF8MjXKY","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01QgqKcp1kXjEV5J9fRter7T":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/vv/zyff93v5391cmw7j8mlcf1ym0000gn/T/wi-agent-ptoywky0/NOTES.md","content":"# Algorithm\n\nLet s = x[1] + x[5] + x[9] + x[14], an integer from 0 to 4. The label is s mod 2.\n\n- **Layer 1:** units 0..3 compute r_k = relu(s - k) for k = 0, 1, 2, 3. Each has weight 1 on the four relevant bits and bias -k. All other units are zero.\n- **Layer 2:** for integer s in [0, 4], parity is exactly `odd = r0 - 2 r1 + 2 r2 - 2 r3`. Checking each value: s=0→0, s=1→1, s=2→0, s=3→1, s=4→0. Unit 0 = relu(odd) and unit 1 = relu(1 - odd). Both values are already 0 or 1, so the ReLU changes nothing.\n- **Output:** logit1 = 10·odd and logit0 = 10·(1 − odd). The argmax is the parity, with a margin of 10. The distractor bits have zero weight everywhere.\n\nThe network should be 100% accurate on all 2^16 inputs.\n"}}}
